%I A175554 #13 Aug 10 2026 00:53:50
%S A175554 1,6,960,40037760,905697107804160
%N A175554 Number of Hamiltonian cycle decompositions of the complete graph on 2n+1 vertices.
%C A175554 There are 10!/2 = 1814400 Hamiltonian cycles in K_11. For a fixed cycle, its complement has 2495858432 decompositions into four Hamiltonian cycles. Since each decomposition of K_11 contains five cycles, double-counting gives a(5) = (1814400/5)*2495858432 = 905697107804160, independently verifying Mutoh's value. - _Siddhartha Mahajan_, Aug 09 2026
%H A175554 Nobuaki Mutoh, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1002/jcd.70017">On Kotzig's Perfect Set Problem of Hamiltonian Cycle Decompositions of the Complete Graph</a>, Journal of Combinatorial Designs, 34 (2026), no. 8, 388-409.
%H A175554 Douglas S. Stones, <a href="https://mathoverflow.net/questions/10577/hamilton-cycle-decompositions-of-the-complete-graph">Hamilton cycle decompositions of the complete graph</a>, MathOverflow.
%K A175554 nonn,hard,more
%O A175554 1,2
%A A175554 _Max Alekseyev_, Jun 28 2010
%E A175554 a(1)-a(4) were computed by Douglas S. Stones.
%E A175554 a(5) from Nobuaki Mutoh (2026), independently verified by _Siddhartha Mahajan_, Aug 09 2026
